Z||000000||Fformula88||12-05-2000||08:07 PM||||Does anybody have the GM service manual for their Fiero?  I was wondering if its worth the price to have.  I have a Haynes manual now and have been very happy with it, but am also planning on keeping my Fiero for a long time.  So I was considering making the investment.  Is it worth it?  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||12-05-2000||08:30 PM||||I have both Factory and Haynes. I find myself referring to the factory more often for electrical and emission problems. These are more comprehensive in the factory manual and offer better troubleshooting charts. Also the factory manual seems to have more views and illustrations then the Haynes.<BR>The Haynes manual is the best non-factory manual i've seen. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
